msgid "The weak default returns and has no state or side effects. A product may supply one strong implementation, bounded and allocation-free in every calling task/ISR/masked context. No functioning kernel, clock, stack, transport or peripheral may be assumed after corruption. This is best-effort observation, not stack repair, safe outputs or reset proof. The hook must not acquire OS locks, reenter the provider, change incoming masks, mutate accepted requests or release retained storage. If it returns, the terminal caller still parks. A product may perform a separately reviewed non-returning recovery action. No retained event, registry or worker is implicit."
msgstr "The weak default returns and has no state or side effects. A product may supply one strong implementation, bounded and allocation-free in every calling task/ISR/masked context. No functioning kernel, clock, stack, transport or peripheral may be assumed after corruption. This is best-effort observation, not stack repair, safe outputs or reset proof. The hook must not acquire OS locks, reenter the provider, change incoming masks, mutate accepted requests or release retained storage. If it returns, the terminal caller still parks. A product may perform a separately reviewed non-returning recovery action. No retained event, registry or worker is implicit."

