msgid "Use these attributes on variable definitions, before the type, one variable per declaration. They are not function or instruction attributes. Each use has an independent input section for garbage collection of unused storage. DATA copies its initializer from Flash at reset. BSS is zeroed at reset. NOINIT is neither copied nor cleared; initialize it before reading. Power-loss retention is not promised. BSS/NOINIT reject nonzero initializers. Storage is word aligned and subject to explicit ELF budgets. Unselected use is a compile error. TCM is CPU-only data: never DMA or executable storage. CCM is also CPU-only data; placement never grants bus-master access. ADDSRAM DMA requires provider address, alignment and ownership validation. Ordinary storage, the main MSP and unselected images keep their existing layout."
msgstr "Use these attributes on variable definitions, before the type, one variable per declaration. They are not function or instruction attributes. Each use has an independent input section for garbage collection of unused storage. DATA copies its initializer from Flash at reset. BSS is zeroed at reset. NOINIT is neither copied nor cleared; initialize it before reading. Power-loss retention is not promised. BSS/NOINIT reject nonzero initializers. Storage is word aligned and subject to explicit ELF budgets. Unselected use is a compile error. TCM is CPU-only data: never DMA or executable storage. CCM is also CPU-only data; placement never grants bus-master access. ADDSRAM DMA requires provider address, alignment and ownership validation. Ordinary storage, the main MSP and unselected images keep their existing layout."

