msgid "Physical providers require successful platform startup and a privileged task/configurable IRQ; NMI/HardFault callers are unsupported. No OS, allocation or wait. Physical clocks return zero outside a successfully started live epoch; zero alone cannot prove readiness. Startup status is authoritative. All consumers join before clock withdrawal. Stop/restart or a clock change invalidates every old deadline, even if a new epoch has the same numerical value. UINT64_MAX is reserved; clock exhaustion requires controlled restart. An observed hardware overflow acknowledgement failure ends the live epoch and is terminal, even when finite source isolation succeeds. The provider retains ownership, masks interrupts, calls nx_fault_observe and parks if the observer returns. It never resumes deadline consumers with invalid zero time. Observation neither releases loans nor proves safe outputs; products own separately reviewed non-returning recovery. Ordinary shutdown still requires every consumer and optional low-power owner joined first."
msgstr "Physical providers require successful platform startup and a privileged task/configurable IRQ; NMI/HardFault callers are unsupported. No OS, allocation or wait. Physical clocks return zero outside a successfully started live epoch; zero alone cannot prove readiness. Startup status is authoritative. All consumers join before clock withdrawal. Stop/restart or a clock change invalidates every old deadline, even if a new epoch has the same numerical value. UINT64_MAX is reserved; clock exhaustion requires controlled restart. An observed hardware overflow acknowledgement failure ends the live epoch and is terminal, even when finite source isolation succeeds. The provider retains ownership, masks interrupts, calls nx_fault_observe and parks if the observer returns. It never resumes deadline consumers with invalid zero time. Observation neither releases loans nor proves safe outputs; products own separately reviewed non-returning recovery. Ordinary shutdown still requires every consumer and optional low-power owner joined first."

